{"id":"u-58b541d8-296b-4f4a-a496-6e5f265019fd","src":"community","title":"High School Rugby Offseason Strength","author":"Samuel C.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/xDxhj1-high-school-rugby-offseason-strength","desc":"The High School Rugby Offseason Strength program is designed to develop foundational strength, movement quality, and athletic durability in young rugby athletes. Across four structured training days each week, players will learn to move efficiently under load, brace through contact, and recover between efforts — all while keeping technique and posture at the forefront.\n\nThis program emphasizes simplicity, safety, and rugby-specific strength:\n\nZercher squats teach core bracing and upright posture for tackling and scrummaging.\n\nIncline presses build upper-body power and shoulder stability for contact.\n\nRack pulls develop posterior chain strength and lockout power crucial for rucks and mauls.\n\nAerobic work capacity days enhance recovery, endurance, and mental toughness.\n\nBy keeping the structure low complexity but high intent, the goal is to help athletes become resilient, explosive, and technically sound — strong enough to dominate collisions and conditioned enough to outlast the opposition.\n\nThis is not about lifting the heaviest weight possible — it’s about mastering movement, building habits, and developing the kind of strength that shows up on the field.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":40,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-07-28T18:06:22.133Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Lower Body","Upper Body","Full Body","Aerobic/Work Capacity"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Band Pull Apart","sets":[{"r":15,"x":2}]},{"n":"T Spine Rotations","sets":[{"r":5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Cossack Squat (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":5,"x":2}]}]},{"n":"Box Jump","sets":[{"r":3,"x":3}]},{"n":"Zercher Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":3,"hi":6,"rpe":6,"x":4}]},{"